That error is expected, and nothing is broken.What happened
~/.cli-proxy-api/free-keys.conf is a settings file, not a program.
The script made it with chmod 600, so it has no execute bit → Permission denied. 
Even if it were executable, running it would only set variables inside a throwaway shell and then exit. It would do nothing useful. 
The script told you the right move: edit it, then run ~/cpa-free.What to do next
1. Open the file in an editor

